      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This clinical study retrospectively compared the relationship of anginal attack during dental extractions with factors such as blood pressure, heart rate, rate-pressure product, and electrocardiographic findings. The anesthetic procedure produced the greatest change in the various parameters. No direct relationship could be observed between anginal attack and doses of lidocaine, epinephrine, and premedicative drug or time required for treatment."},
